#: ../../source/mp/l2_storage/valkey.rst:2
msgid "Valkey"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mp/l2_storage/valkey.rst:4
msgid ""
"An L2 adapter backed by the official ``valkey-glide`` **sync** Python "
"client. Stores KV cache chunks in a Valkey (or Redis) server and supports"
" both **standalone** (``GlideClient``) and **Valkey-Cluster** "
"(``GlideClusterClient``) topologies, selected via ``cluster_mode``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mp/l2_storage/valkey.rst:9
msgid ""
"I/O is dispatched through an internal ``ValkeyWorkerPool`` of worker "
"threads; each worker holds its own glide client so a batch of keys "
"parallelizes across threads and (in cluster mode) across primaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mp/l2_storage/valkey.rst:14
msgid "Why the ``valkey`` adapter (vs. the RESP adapter)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mp/l2_storage/valkey.rst:16
msgid ""
"The :doc:`RESP <resp>` adapter targets a single Redis/Valkey server over "
"the native C++ RESP connector. The ``valkey`` adapter is a first-class "
"Valkey backend: it speaks ``valkey-glide-sync`` directly, adds Valkey-"
"Cluster support (slot routing, MOVED/ASK redirects, and topology "
"discovery are handled inside ``GlideClusterClient``), and preserves copy-"
"reduced SET/GET on multi-megabyte KV chunks (see the `Valkey L2 Adapter "
"design doc "
"<https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/docs/design/v1/distributed/l2_adapters/valkey.md>`_"
" for the full rationale, including why the sync -- not async -- glide "
"client is used)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mp/l2_storage/valkey.rst:28
msgid "Prerequisites -- installing the glide sync client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mp/l2_storage/valkey.rst:30
msgid ""
